A map of every device on the networks of the firewall, with how it is
connected, how much it talks and what the firewall does with its traffic.

* Devices from host discovery, DHCP leases and the ARP table, grouped by
  network (VLAN), with their kind guessed from name and manufacturer.
* When the Instant On plugin is installed: the physical tree with
  switches, access points, cable or Wi-Fi links, port, speed and signal.
* Live traffic per device from the firewall state table, with remote
  hosts named from the DNS resolver cache.
* Packets blocked by the firewall for each device, with the rule.
* Traffic volume history from Insight (NetFlow) when it is enabled.

The plugin only reads.

